.TH RECIPE-HELPERS 7 "2026-11-16" "Recipe" "Recipe Helpers"
.SH NAME
recipe-helpers \- registered managed Rhai helpers
.SH DESCRIPTION
Helpers are called from a recipe's functions (build, configure, verify, latest,
cleanup; see recipe-recipe(5)). A recipe that can reach a helper that starts a
program runs in the configured Ginux domain; any other recipe runs on the host,
where the program helpers are not registered and every file helper is confined
to the run's own directories. Network access requires NEEDS.network grants.
Native errors fail the run. An interrupted step starts again from its beginning;
there is no save, saved, checkpoint or reached. The registered list is src/helpers/mod.rs; there are no ready or
needs_work helpers, because there are no readiness checks.
