\fBcarry_libraries(package, prefix, search:Array) -> Array\fR
Experimental. Copies into package/lib/ the loader and every shared library that
the programs in package/bin/, and the programs and plug-ins the recipe put
under package/lib/, load, from the search folders and then the build image,
and writes into each file its loader and library folder under prefix
(pass PREFIX). A file linked with carry_link_flags() is
settled in its reserved room; any other (an upstream prebuilt release) is
rewritten with a new loadable segment holding the loader path and
$ORIGIN-relative library folders. The C library comes whole from the first
search folder holding its loader, else the build image. Fails unless every
program and file under package/lib/ then finds each library it needs, with
the symbol versions it asks for, inside the package. 64-bit x86_64 only.
.TP
\fBcarry_link_flags() -> String\fR
Experimental. Linker flags for every program and library of a package: a long
stand-in library folder that reserves the room carry_libraries writes into.
