.SH COMMANDS
.PP
Target filesystem helpers retain logical metadata separately from writable staging:
target_extract_tar(archive, root), target_extract_rpm(archive, root),
target_extract_apk(archive, root),
target_capture_apks(root, archive_directories), target_mode(root, relative_path, mode)
and target_finalize(root). RPM extraction reads the package natively (no rpm or rpm2archive);
it does not run package scriptlets. target_extract_apk(archive, root) extracts the
data segment of an Alpine .apk (its signature and control segments, with the install
scripts, are skipped) and records modes, owner names and links the same way.
Both record owners by name only and read no account file, so they run on the host.
Capture package metadata before policy,
then finalize the tree after policy changes. Recipe finishes a tree for a system output itself, so a recipe does not call
target_finalize on one; the options form target_finalize(root, #{ owners: "apply",
accounts: [LINES], seed: "var" }) is what that finishing does:
owner names stay in the manifest and are resolved in the root the system change writes;
seed: "var" keeps var/ as state seeds created there only where missing; accounts is an
optional list of sysusers.d "u"/"u!"/"g"/"m" lines (for Alpine packages, whose install scripts would have
added them), created there together with the tree's own usr/lib/sysusers.d accounts.
target_extract_rpm(archive, root, members) also writes the record of the
extraction to members, from which a package is composed into another root.
target_pack_tree(root, archive) moves a staging tree, its modes, times, links
and target metadata manifest, into a new tar archive, removing root;
target_unpack_tree(archive, root) makes that tree again under an empty root,
as one Ginux archive import stream where the domain offers it and member by
member otherwise, with the same result.
See docs/target-metadata.md.
exec returns a status; exec_checked and exec_output fail on nonzero exit.
Their optional options map accepts child-only cwd and env. Shell strings need
proper quoting and checked pipelines. Diagnostics go to stderr.
.SH PATHS AND OUTPUTS
Use WORK for build material and the paths INPUTS, DEPS and out (build) or tree
(configure) give. Inputs are read-only. On a host run paths outside the run's
own directories, and paths using .., are refused. Select nothing: the output is
the folder or file Recipe hands to build, and the coordinator validates it before
publication and returns its published host path in the result's outputs.
.SH ACQUISITION
Prefer the SOURCES declaration. Downloads inside build require SHA256 and replace
a valid destination only after complete verification. Git acquisition requires an
exact destination and full commit id. Every redirect endpoint also needs a network
grant. Package facts stay in the recipe.
